# Push after testing

When a coding task is implemented and the relevant checks have passed, commit the source changes and push them to the tracked remote.

- Do this at the end of the task, without waiting for a separate push request.
- Leave out local screenshots, audit images, and secret files.
- Do not force-push, skip hooks, or change git config.
- If the push fails because of authentication or a rejected update, say so and stop.
